Article 21

Regional Government must carry out prevention of violence against children which includes:

a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.

Article 45

(1) Every Person in Charge of a business and/or activity that operates internet services, play stations and types of children's games based on information and communication technology shall be obligated to manage and design a child-friendly place.

(2) Provisions as referred to in paragraph (1) include: a. arranging rooms/booths with adequate lighting and not enclosed;

b. not accepting children wearing uniforms and/or during school hours;

c. locally blocking sites containing elements of pornography and pornographic acts; and

d. limiting visiting hours and supervising the use of available facilities.

Article 24

Sexual violence as referred to in Article 21 letter c is caused by:

a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual relations;
c. forced sexual relations in an unnatural or undesirable manner; and/or d. forced sexual relations with others for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes.

